WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.546
Fala was bent over a tubular device when Zann and his friends walked in.

2
00:00:04.547 --> 00:00:08.337
"You're alive!" she cried, rushing over to hug them.

3
00:00:08.338 --> 00:00:11.743
"When I got back here and you were gone, I feared the worst!"

4
00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:16.063
"Sorry," Perda said sheepishly. "We should've left you a note."

5
00:00:16.064 --> 00:00:18.682
Fala stepped back and glared at them.

6
00:00:18.683 --> 00:00:26.201
"Yes, you should have," she scolded. "Never mind—I'm just glad you're okay. But we have a problem." "You're

7
00:00:26.202 --> 00:00:30.223
right," Zann said. "We were just at the palace." "What's

8
00:00:30.224 --> 00:00:33.135
going on at the palace?" asked Fala. Zann

9
00:00:33.136 --> 00:00:36.459
and the others told Fala what had happened. Fala

10
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.761
nodded when they got to the part about Morb appearing in the throne room. "One

11
00:00:40.762 --> 00:00:44.890
of my contacts at the palace was supposed to check in an hour ago. When

12
00:00:44.891 --> 00:00:48.377
I didn't hear from him, I used the Remote Eye." She

13
00:00:48.378 --> 00:00:54.805
gestured at the device. "I saw Morb walking around in the throne room. But

14
00:00:54.806 --> 00:00:58.604
the Eye doesn't have sound, so I couldn't hear what he was saying." "Did

15
00:00:58.605 --> 00:01:01.385
you see Yog?" Zann asked. "No,"

16
00:01:01.386 --> 00:01:04.550
Fala replied. "I hope he's safe. And

17
00:01:04.551 --> 00:01:07.354
I'm glad you kids got out when you did." "We

18
00:01:07.355 --> 00:01:12.479
almost didn't," Gliss told her. "We ran into a troll on our way out." "Well,

19
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.893
Zann did, anyway," Perda added. That

20
00:01:15.894 --> 00:01:20.180
reminded Zann of the silver talisman. He described it to Fala. "Do

21
00:01:20.181 --> 00:01:26.381
you think Morb could be using talismans to send extra power to the trolls?" he asked. "That

22
00:01:26.382 --> 00:01:31.311
sounds like something I've seen in the ancient texts." Fala looked intrigued. "Such

23
00:01:31.312 --> 00:01:38.207
talismans wouldn't only provide extra power—they could also be a way for Morb to control the trolls. If only

24
00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:44.796
we could get our hands on one of those talismans. It could be invaluable to us." "Yeah, well,

25
00:01:44.797 --> 00:01:51.266
good luck finding someone crazy enough to go up to a troll and take it," said Perda. "So what

26
00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:54.867
should we do now?" Zann asked Fala. "We freed

27
00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:57.478
a lot of Reds earlier. If we

28
00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:01.788
all work together, maybe we can stop Morb." Fala looked

29
00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:09.593
worried. "Most of those Reds aren't ready to face Morb yet. They're staying hidden, not using magic. Venna and

30
00:02:09.594 --> 00:02:13.580
her people are trying to devise a plan." She shrugged. "Maybe you

31
00:02:13.581 --> 00:02:18.440
kids should head home—you'll be safer there until we figure out what to do. Do you

32
00:02:18.441 --> 00:02:20.488
have a way to get there?" "We rode

33
00:02:20.489 --> 00:02:25.197
here on dragons," Darb said. "We left them grazing in the forest." "We're not

34
00:02:25.198 --> 00:02:29.932
going home—I don't have a home to go to," Zann said. "My grandfather

35
00:02:29.933 --> 00:02:33.942
was taken and so were Gliss' parents." Gliss nodded.

36
00:02:33.943 --> 00:02:39.855
"Swamp Bottom isn't any safer than First City. We're staying here." "All right,"

37
00:02:39.856 --> 00:02:44.492
said Fala. "But it's getting late—let's get some sleep. Tomorrow could

38
00:02:44.493 --> 00:02:47.793
be a very long day." Late that

39
00:02:47.794 --> 00:02:52.028
night Morb stood alone in the palace courtyard. Sweat poured

40
00:02:52.029 --> 00:02:56.739
off his forehead as he focused every bit of energy he could gather. "Come

41
00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:00.340
to me," he murmured. His

42
00:03:00.341 --> 00:03:07.635
entire body shook with effort. With the magic he'd taken from all those Reds, was he strong enough to do this? His

43
00:03:07.636 --> 00:03:11.800
energy began to waver. Sharp pains were shooting through him. But

44
00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:17.380
he'd waited too long for this moment—he wouldn't wait any longer. It had to be now! Morb's

45
00:03:17.381 --> 00:03:21.952
knees buckled as he focused every ounce of energy on his task. Falling

46
00:03:21.953 --> 00:03:25.700
to the ground, he writhed back and forth in agony. And

47
00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:31.641
that was all it took. The extra bit of friction shot through him. "Yes!"

48
00:03:31.642 --> 00:03:36.055
he gasped as he felt his energy shift. Crash

49
00:03:36.056 --> 00:03:37.080
!

50
00:03:37.081 --> 00:03:39.797
His eyes popped open and he smiled.

51
00:03:39.798 --> 00:03:45.233
His masterpiece, the new machine, stood before him in all its evil glory.

52
00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:53.817
Its enormous frame of wire and bone gleamed in the starlight, and the paralyzer pythons writhed angrily in their glass prison.

53
00:03:53.818 --> 00:03:59.666
Morb climbed to his feet, still shaking from the effort of moving the machine all the way from the fortress.

54
00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:02.579
For a moment he considered summoning Wyssa.

55
00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:09.358
He only needed a few more items, starting with the Skellian sea sponge she'd promised to bring him tomorrow.

56
00:04:09.359 --> 00:04:13.822
If he ordered her to fetch it now, the machine would be complete that much sooner.

57
00:04:13.823 --> 00:04:18.204
But he decided to wait. After all, what was one more day?

58
00:04:18.205 --> 00:04:24.816
Very soon now, he would have everything he'd ever dreamed of back in his pathetic Void days.

59
00:04:24.817 --> 00:04:31.880
When Zann awoke the next morning, his friends were eating puckerberry pancakes. Zing was slurping dragon mush nearby.

60
00:04:31.881 --> 00:04:35.524
"We didn't want to wake you," Perda said when Zann sat up.

61
00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:38.268
"We figured you needed the extra sleep."

62
00:04:38.269 --> 00:04:42.653
Darb grinned. "Plus Perda wanted to eat all your pancakes."

63
00:04:42.654 --> 00:04:47.289
Zann hurried over to them. "Where's Fala?" he asked, grabbing some food.

64
00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:50.631
"She was gone when we woke up," Gliss said.

65
00:04:50.632 --> 00:04:54.379
"She left a note telling us to stay here until she gets back."

66
00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:59.047
Zann didn't say anything. He finished his breakfast and then headed toward the door.

67
00:04:59.048 --> 00:05:01.919
"Where are you going?" Perda asked.

68
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.621
"I want to see what's going on outside," Zann replied.

69
00:05:05.622 --> 00:05:10.487
When he turned the doorknob, it started spinning so fast that he couldn't hold onto it.

70
00:05:10.488 --> 00:05:13.812
Then a little toy bird popped into view.

71
00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:17.162
"Nice try, kids," it said in Fala's voice.

72
00:05:17.163 --> 00:05:24.122
The others laughed, but Zann frowned. He thought about trying to find a way to breach Fala's spell.

73
00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:27.064
But without using magic, it seemed hopeless.

74
00:05:27.065 --> 00:05:32.251
He realized he had no choice but to stay there as she'd asked—at least for a little while.

75
00:05:32.252 --> 00:05:37.295
Luckily he didn't have to wait too long. Fala burst in 15 minutes later.

76
00:05:37.296 --> 00:05:41.413
"What's wrong?" Zann asked when he saw the grim look on her face.

77
00:05:41.414 --> 00:05:50.788
"I've been out gathering the latest news," Fala replied. "It's not good."

